# Stage1 backend — the SWITCH a scalar `match` statement lowers to: one comparison chain over
# the scrutinee, an arm block per case, and the default that closes it. Reached from
# codegen_stmt_match_scalar.elisa, which handles the string and sview scrutinees first.
# Part of `module Backend` (see codegen.elisa).

extend Backend:
    private:
        def emit_statement_match_switch(stmt_match_scrutinee: Expr, sm_scrutinee_type: ValueType, sm_penum: bool, stmt_match_arms: darray[MatchArm]&, return_type: ValueType, local_scope: mutable Scope&, loops: mutable LoopStack&, regions: mutable RegionStack&, fns: FnTable&, structs: mutable StructTable&, generics: mutable GenericTable&, runtime: Runtime&, m: LLVMModuleRef, ctx: LLVMContextRef, builder: LLVMBuilderRef, handled: mutable bool&) -> EmitStatus can[Abort.Panic, Memory.Allocate, Unsafe.PointerCast]:
            if emit_expression(stmt_match_scrutinee, sm_scrutinee_type, local_scope, fns, structs, generics, runtime, m, ctx, builder) is sm_scrutinee_raw:
                sm_function: LLVMValueRef = LLVMGetBasicBlockParent(LLVMGetInsertBlock(builder))
                sm_scrutinee: mutable LLVMValueRef = sm_scrutinee_raw
                sm_compare_type: mutable LLVMTypeRef = llvm_type_of(sm_scrutinee_type, structs, ctx)
                sm_penum_slot: mutable LLVMValueRef = sm_scrutinee_raw
                if sm_penum:
                    sm_scrutinee <- LLVMBuildExtractValue(builder, sm_scrutinee_raw, 0, "smatch.tag")
                    sm_compare_type <- LLVMInt32TypeInContext(ctx)
                    sm_penum_slot <- build_entry_alloca(builder, llvm_type_of(sm_scrutinee_type, structs, ctx), "smatch.payload.tmp")
                    _ = LLVMBuildStore(builder, sm_scrutinee_raw, sm_penum_slot)
                sm_done: LLVMBasicBlockRef = LLVMAppendBasicBlockInContext(ctx, sm_function, "smatch.done")
                # ONE slot per bound NAME for the whole match, not one per arm. Each arm used
                # to alloca its own, so a binding read AFTER the match loaded the LAST arm's
                # slot — which `opt -passes=verify` rejects ("Instruction does not dominate
                # all uses": the alloca sits in an arm block, the load in smatch.done) and
                # which segfaulted at runtime. A variant that happened to take the last arm
                # answered correctly and still emitted invalid IR, so it was latent wherever
                # arms share a binding name.
                #
                # stage0's rule, measured: the binding SURVIVES the match carrying the taken
                # arm's value (`match e: E.A(v) … ` then `return v` answers 3, not the outer
                # 100) — which is exactly what one shared slot gives. This is the same
                # registry emit_condition opens for an `is` test; bind_is_slot allocates in
                # the ENTRY block, so the slot dominates every use.
                structs.cond_bind_depth <- structs.cond_bind_depth + 1
                sm_declined: mutable bool = false
                sm_saw_default: mutable bool = false
                sm_any_open: mutable bool = false
                for sm_arm in stmt_match_arms |sm_declined, sm_saw_default, sm_any_open, sm_penum, sm_scrutinee, sm_compare_type, sm_penum_slot, sm_scrutinee_type, sm_function, sm_done, return_type, local_scope, loops, regions, fns, structs, generics, runtime, m, ctx, builder|:
                    continue if sm_declined or sm_saw_default
                    sm_ordinal: mutable i64 = -1
                    # A NEGATIVE literal (`-1:`) is a valid compare value, so `sm_ordinal < 0`
                    # cannot double as the "no value resolved" sentinel; track it explicitly.
                    sm_has_value: mutable bool = false
                    sm_is_default: mutable bool = false
                    sm_payload_binding: mutable sview = ""
                    sm_payload_multi: mutable darray[sview] = []
                    sm_payload_path: mutable sview = ""
                    # NESTED variant sub-patterns in a single-field payload
                    # (`Expr.Leaf(Token.Ident)`, or an alternation
                    # `Expr.Leaf(Token.Ident | Token.Keyword)`): the payload's own tag must
                    # be tested before the arm runs. Empty when the arm has no nested
                    # pattern; more than one entry means the tests are OR-ed.
                    sm_nested_paths: mutable darray[sview] = []
                    # The binder of a nested variant that carries a payload, or "".
                    sm_nested_binder: mutable sview = ""
                    sm_is_range: mutable bool = false
                    sm_range_lo: mutable sview = ""
                    sm_range_hi: mutable sview = ""
                    sm_range_inclusive: mutable bool = false
                    sm_is_or: mutable bool = false
                    sm_or_options: mutable darray[Pattern] = []
                    sm_is_pin: mutable bool = false
                    sm_pin_name: mutable sview = ""
                    # docs/77 §2 CATEGORY ARM (`InputEvent input:`): dispatch is the docs/81
                    # range primitive over the category's leaf-tag span, and the binder is the
                    # same value at the narrowed static type -- a refinement is an alias of its
                    # root, so that re-bind is a no-op store.
                    sm_is_category: mutable bool = false
                    sm_category_lo: mutable i64 = 0
                    sm_category_count: mutable i64 = 0
                    sm_category_binder: mutable sview = ""
                    if sm_penum and sm_arm.pattern is Pattern.TypeBind(sm_category_type, sm_category_bound):
                        # A PayloadEnum ValueType carries its registry index in `bits`.
                        if penum_category_tag_range(structs, sm_scrutinee_type.bits.i64(), sm_category_type, sm_category_lo, sm_category_count):
                            sm_is_category <- true
                            sm_category_binder <- sm_category_bound
                    # `Shape.Circle(r) as whole:` — docs/122 §5.4 as-binding. The parser only
                    # ever wraps a Variant or Struct pattern in Pattern.As, so unwrapping it
                    # here (Variant is the only shape this scalar-enum arm loop deals with)
                    # and testing the inner pattern below covers it with no new dispatch shape.
                    sm_as_name: mutable sview = ""
                    sm_pattern: mutable Pattern = sm_arm.pattern
                    if sm_arm.pattern is Pattern.As(sm_as_outer_name, sm_as_inner):
                        if sm_as_inner.count == 1 and sm_as_inner[0] is Pattern.Variant(_, _):
                            sm_as_name <- sm_as_outer_name
                            sm_pattern <- sm_as_inner[0]
                    if sm_arm.pattern is Pattern.Literal(sm_literal_text):
                        sm_literal_value: mutable i64 = 0
                        if parse_pattern_scalar(sm_literal_text, sm_literal_value):
                            sm_ordinal <- sm_literal_value
                            sm_has_value <- true
                        else:
                            sm_declined <- true
                    if sm_pattern is Pattern.Variant(sm_path, sm_fields):
                        sm_payload_path <- sm_path
                        if sm_penum:
                            sm_ordinal <- penum_variant_index_of_path(sm_path, structs)
                            if sm_fields.count == 1:
                                if sm_fields[0] is Pattern.Binding(sm_bound):
                                    sm_payload_binding <- sm_bound
                                elif sm_fields[0] is Pattern.Field(sm_sole_label, sm_sole_subs):
                                    # `Just(value: inner)` — the single-field payload written with
                                    # its label. One field, so the label carries no ordering
                                    # information; it only has to name that field.
                                    sm_sole_slot: i64 = penum_slot_of_path(sm_path, structs)
                                    if sm_sole_slot < 0 or sm_sole_subs.count != 1:
                                        sm_declined <- true
                                    elif sm_sole_subs[0] is Pattern.Binding(sm_sole_bound):
                                        sm_sole_ok: mutable bool = false
                                        sm_sole_start: usize = structs.penum_field_type_start[sm_sole_slot.usize()]
                                        for sm_sole_probe in 0..<structs.penum_field_type_count[sm_sole_slot.usize()] |sm_sole_ok, sm_sole_label, sm_sole_start, structs|:
                                            sm_sole_ok <- true if structs.penum_field_flat_names[sm_sole_start + sm_sole_probe] == sm_sole_label
                                        if sm_sole_ok:
                                            sm_payload_binding <- sm_sole_bound
                                        else:
                                            sm_declined <- true
                                    else:
                                        sm_declined <- true
                                elif sm_fields[0] is Pattern.Variant(sm_nested_variant_path, sm_nested_variant_fields):
                                    # `Expr.Leaf(Token.Ident)` — a PAYLOADLESS nested variant.
                                    # Record it; the tag test is emitted inside the arm block
                                    # below. A nested variant that itself BINDS still declines:
                                    # its sub-fields would have to be read too, and matching
                                    # without testing them is a wrong answer, not a drop.
                                    if sm_nested_variant_fields.count == 0:
                                        sm_nested_paths.push(sm_nested_variant_path)
                                    elif sm_nested_variant_fields.count == 1 and sm_nested_variant_fields[0] is Pattern.Binding(sm_nested_bound):
                                        # `Outer.Wrap(Inner.A(inner))` — a nested variant that
                                        # CARRIES a payload and binds it. Its tag lives inside
                                        # the nested aggregate rather than being the payload
                                        # word itself, so it is recorded separately from the
                                        # payloadless paths above and tested/bound below.
                                        sm_nested_paths.push(sm_nested_variant_path)
                                        sm_nested_binder <- sm_nested_bound
                                    else:
                                        sm_declined <- true
                                elif sm_fields[0] is Pattern.Or(sm_nested_options):
                                    # `Expr.Leaf(Token.Ident | Token.Keyword)` — an alternation
                                    # of payloadless nested variants. Every option must be one,
                                    # or the whole arm declines; the tests are OR-ed below.
                                    for sm_nested_option in sm_nested_options |sm_nested_paths, sm_nested_binder, sm_declined|:
                                        sm_option_ok: mutable bool = false
                                        if sm_nested_option is Pattern.Variant(sm_option_path, sm_option_fields):
                                            if sm_option_fields.count == 0:
                                                sm_nested_paths.push(sm_option_path)
                                                sm_option_ok <- true
                                            # `Token.Ident(value) | Token.Keyword(value)` — an
                                            # alternation whose options CARRY payloads and bind
                                            # one name. This was implemented, verified correct,
                                            # and then REVERTED because stage0 MISCOMPILED the
                                            # shape: it bound a constant for the second option,
                                            # so a correct lowering read as a differential
                                            # MISMATCH against a wrong oracle.
                                            #
                                            # stage0 is now FIXED (its payload spill did not
                                            # dominate the later option blocks), so the reason
                                            # for declining is gone. Every option binds the
                                            # SAME name into ONE slot, and the payload-type
                                            # agreement check below rejects options whose
                                            # payload types differ -- one binder cannot hold
                                            # two types. Options binding DIFFERENT names would
                                            # need one slot each, which this arm shape cannot
                                            # express, so that still declines.
                                            elif sm_option_fields.count == 1 and sm_option_fields[0] is Pattern.Binding(sm_option_bound):
                                                if sm_nested_binder == "" or sm_nested_binder == sm_option_bound:
                                                    sm_nested_paths.push(sm_option_path)
                                                    sm_nested_binder <- sm_option_bound
                                                    sm_option_ok <- true
                                        sm_declined <- true if not sm_option_ok
                                else:
                                    sm_declined <- true
                            if sm_fields.count > 1:
                                # LABELLED payload patterns (`Pair(right: r, left: l)`) arrive as
                                # Pattern.Field(label, [Binding]) and may be written in ANY order,
                                # while the bind loop below indexes binders by DECLARED position.
                                # Resolve each label to its declared index and fill that slot;
                                # unlabelled fields fill positionally, so the plain spelling is
                                # unchanged. A label that names no field, or a duplicate, leaves a
                                # hole and declines rather than binding the wrong field.
                                sm_label_slot: i64 = penum_slot_of_path(sm_path, structs)
                                if sm_label_slot < 0:
                                    sm_declined <- true
                                else:
                                    sm_label_start: usize = structs.penum_field_type_start[sm_label_slot.usize()]
                                    sm_label_count: usize = structs.penum_field_type_count[sm_label_slot.usize()]
                                    sm_ordered: mutable darray[sview] = ["" for _slot in 0..<sm_label_count]
                                    sm_next_free: mutable usize = 0
                                    for sm_multi_field in sm_fields |sm_ordered, sm_next_free, sm_declined, sm_label_start, sm_label_count, structs|:
                                        if sm_multi_field is Pattern.Binding(sm_multi_bound):
                                            while sm_next_free < sm_label_count and sm_ordered[sm_next_free] != "" |sm_next_free, sm_ordered, sm_label_count|:
                                                sm_next_free <- sm_next_free + 1
                                            if sm_next_free < sm_label_count:
                                                sm_ordered[sm_next_free] <- sm_multi_bound
                                            else:
                                                sm_declined <- true
                                        elif sm_multi_field is Pattern.Field(sm_label_name, sm_label_subs):
                                            sm_label_index: mutable i64 = -1
                                            for sm_label_probe in 0..<sm_label_count |sm_label_index, sm_label_name, sm_label_start, structs|:
                                                sm_label_index <- sm_label_probe.i64() if structs.penum_field_flat_names[sm_label_start + sm_label_probe] == sm_label_name
                                            if sm_label_index < 0 or sm_label_subs.count != 1:
                                                sm_declined <- true
                                            elif sm_label_subs[0] is Pattern.Binding(sm_label_bound):
                                                if sm_ordered[sm_label_index.usize()] == "":
                                                    sm_ordered[sm_label_index.usize()] <- sm_label_bound
                                                else:
                                                    sm_declined <- true
                                            else:
                                                sm_declined <- true
                                        else:
                                            sm_declined <- true
                                    for sm_ordered_name in sm_ordered |sm_payload_multi, sm_declined|:
                                        sm_declined <- true if sm_ordered_name == ""
                                        sm_payload_multi.push(sm_ordered_name)
                        else:
                            sm_declined <- true if sm_fields.count != 0
                            sm_ordinal <- ordinal_of_dotted_path(sm_path, structs) if sm_fields.count == 0
                        sm_declined <- true if sm_ordinal < 0
                        sm_has_value <- true if sm_ordinal >= 0
                    if sm_arm.pattern is Pattern.Range(sm_rlo, sm_rhi, sm_rincl):
                        # Range arms are integer-only; a payload-enum tag has no range.
                        sm_declined <- true if sm_penum
                        sm_is_range <- true if not sm_penum
                        sm_range_lo <- sm_rlo
                        sm_range_hi <- sm_rhi
                        sm_range_inclusive <- sm_rincl
                    if sm_arm.pattern is Pattern.Or(sm_opts):
                        sm_is_or <- true
                        sm_or_options <- sm_opts
                    if sm_arm.pattern is Pattern.Pin(sm_pin_binding_name):
                        # A pinned tag compare has no established shape yet; decline rather
                        # than guessing at a payload-enum's ordinal semantics.
                        sm_declined <- true if sm_penum
                        sm_is_pin <- true if not sm_penum
                        sm_pin_name <- sm_pin_binding_name
                    sm_is_default <- true if is_catch_all_pattern(sm_arm.pattern)
                    sm_declined <- true if not sm_has_value and not sm_is_default and not sm_is_range and not sm_is_or and not sm_is_pin and not sm_is_category
                    continue if sm_declined
                    sm_arm_block: LLVMBasicBlockRef = LLVMAppendBasicBlockInContext(ctx, sm_function, "smatch.arm")
                    if arm_has_guard(sm_arm.guard) and sm_is_default:
                        sm_declined <- true
                        continue
                    if sm_is_default:
                        _ = LLVMBuildBr(builder, sm_arm_block)
                        LLVMPositionBuilderAtEnd(builder, sm_arm_block)
                        sm_default_status: EmitStatus = emit_statements(sm_arm.body, return_type, local_scope, loops, regions, fns, structs, generics, runtime, m, ctx, builder)
                        sm_declined <- true if sm_default_status == EmitStatus.Declined
                        sm_any_open <- true if sm_default_status == EmitStatus.Open
                        branch_if_open(sm_default_status, builder, sm_done)
                        sm_saw_default <- true if sm_default_status != EmitStatus.Declined
                    else:
                        sm_next_block: LLVMBasicBlockRef = LLVMAppendBasicBlockInContext(ctx, sm_function, "smatch.next")
                        sm_hit: mutable LLVMValueRef = zeroed
                        if sm_is_range:
                            if emit_range_test(sm_scrutinee, sm_scrutinee_type, sm_range_lo, sm_range_hi, sm_range_inclusive, sm_compare_type, ctx, builder) is sm_range_hit:
                                sm_hit <- sm_range_hit
                            else:
                                sm_declined <- true
                        elif sm_is_or:
                            if emit_or_pattern_hit(sm_or_options, sm_scrutinee, sm_scrutinee_type, sm_penum, sm_compare_type, structs, ctx, builder) is sm_or_hit:
                                sm_hit <- sm_or_hit
                            else:
                                sm_declined <- true
                        elif sm_is_category:
                            # tag - lo <u count. count == 1 folds to equality (a leaf is a
                            # range of one); lo == 0 skips the subtract.
                            sm_cat_lo_const: LLVMValueRef = LLVMConstInt(sm_compare_type, sm_category_lo.u64(), 0)
                            if sm_category_count == 1:
                                sm_hit <- LLVMBuildICmp(builder, 32, sm_scrutinee, sm_cat_lo_const, "smatch.cat.eq")
                            else:
                                sm_cat_rel: LLVMValueRef = LLVMBuildSub(builder, sm_scrutinee, sm_cat_lo_const, "smatch.cat.rel") if sm_category_lo != 0 else sm_scrutinee
                                sm_hit <- LLVMBuildICmp(builder, 36, sm_cat_rel, LLVMConstInt(sm_compare_type, sm_category_count.u64(), 0), "smatch.cat.range")
                        elif sm_is_pin:
                            # `^target:` — compare the scrutinee against the pinned name's
                            # value: an already-bound local's current value, or a `const`'s
                            # folded one. Declines if it is neither; codegen must not guess.
                            if pin_compare_operand(sm_pin_name, sm_compare_type, local_scope, structs, builder) is sm_pin_operand:
                                sm_hit <- LLVMBuildICmp(builder, 32, sm_scrutinee, sm_pin_operand, "smatch.pin.eq")
                            else:
                                sm_declined <- true
                        else:
                            sm_hit <- LLVMBuildICmp(builder, 32, sm_scrutinee, LLVMConstInt(sm_compare_type, sm_ordinal.u64(), 1), "smatch.cmp")
                        continue if sm_declined
                        _ = LLVMBuildCondBr(builder, sm_hit, sm_arm_block, sm_next_block)
                        LLVMPositionBuilderAtEnd(builder, sm_arm_block)
                        if sm_is_category and sm_category_binder != "":
                            sm_cat_bind_storage: mutable darray[u8] = []
                            sm_cat_bind_slot: LLVMValueRef = build_entry_alloca(builder, llvm_type_of(sm_scrutinee_type, structs, ctx), sview_to_cstr(sm_category_binder, sm_cat_bind_storage))
                            _ = LLVMBuildStore(builder, sm_scrutinee_raw, sm_cat_bind_slot)
                            declare_local(local_scope, sm_category_binder, sm_cat_bind_slot, sm_scrutinee_type)
                        # NESTED variant test (`Expr.Leaf(Token.Ident)`). The outer tag has
                        # matched; now load the payload at ITS OWN type and compare that
                        # value against the nested variant's ordinal, falling through to
                        # sm_next_block on a mismatch. Mirrors stage0's shape exactly
                        # (`match.pattern.ok` -> load payload -> icmp -> `match.pattern.ok3`),
                        # read from its -emit llvm.
                        #
                        # A payloadless enum is a plain scalar, so the loaded value IS the
                        # tag; a payload-carrying nested enum would need its tag extracted
                        # from the aggregate instead, so that shape declines rather than
                        # comparing the wrong bytes.
                        if sm_nested_paths.count > 0 and not sm_declined:
                            sm_nested_payload: ValueType = penum_payload_of_path(sm_payload_path, structs)
                            if sm_nested_payload.kind == TypeKind.PayloadEnum:
                                # The outer payload IS a payload-carrying enum: its tag is
                                # field 0 of the nested aggregate, not the payload word. Test
                                # that, then bind field 1 at the nested variant's own payload
                                # type. Restricted to a SINGLE nested path -- an alternation
                                # over payload-carrying variants would bind different payload
                                # types per option, which one binder cannot express.
                                # Every option's payload type must agree: one binder cannot
                                # hold two different types. The first option's type is the
                                # reference; any divergence declines.
                                sm_np_inner_type: mutable ValueType = unmodeled_type()
                                sm_np_ordinals: mutable darray[i64] = []
                                for sm_np_path in sm_nested_paths |sm_np_ordinals, sm_np_inner_type, sm_declined, sm_nested_binder, structs|:
                                    sm_np_each: i64 = penum_variant_index_of_path(sm_np_path, structs)
                                    if sm_np_each < 0:
                                        sm_declined <- true
                                    else:
                                        sm_np_ordinals.push(sm_np_each)
                                    if sm_nested_binder != "":
                                        sm_np_each_type: ValueType = penum_payload_of_path(sm_np_path, structs)
                                        if sm_np_inner_type.kind == TypeKind.Unmodeled:
                                            sm_np_inner_type <- sm_np_each_type
                                        else:
                                            sm_declined <- true if sm_np_each_type.kind != sm_np_inner_type.kind or sm_np_each_type.bits != sm_np_inner_type.bits
                                if sm_declined or sm_np_ordinals.count == 0:
                                    sm_declined <- true
                                else:
                                    sm_np_llvm: LLVMTypeRef = llvm_type_of(sm_nested_payload, structs, ctx)
                                    sm_np_pointer: LLVMValueRef = LLVMBuildStructGEP2(builder, llvm_type_of(sm_scrutinee_type, structs, ctx), sm_penum_slot, 1, "smatch.np.ptr")
                                    sm_np_value: LLVMValueRef = LLVMBuildLoad2(builder, sm_np_llvm, sm_np_pointer, "smatch.np")
                                    sm_np_tag: LLVMValueRef = LLVMBuildExtractValue(builder, sm_np_value, 0, "smatch.np.tag")
                                    sm_np_hit: mutable LLVMValueRef = zeroed
                                    sm_np_first: mutable bool = true
                                    for sm_np_ord in sm_np_ordinals |sm_np_hit, sm_np_first, sm_np_tag, ctx, builder|:
                                        sm_np_cmp: LLVMValueRef = LLVMBuildICmp(builder, 32, sm_np_tag, LLVMConstInt(LLVMTypeOf(sm_np_tag), sm_np_ord.u64(), 0), "smatch.np.eq")
                                        if sm_np_first:
                                            sm_np_hit <- sm_np_cmp
                                            sm_np_first <- false
                                        else:
                                            sm_np_hit <- LLVMBuildOr(builder, sm_np_hit, sm_np_cmp, "smatch.np.or")
                                    sm_np_ok: LLVMBasicBlockRef = LLVMAppendBasicBlockInContext(ctx, sm_function, "smatch.np.ok")
                                    _ = LLVMBuildCondBr(builder, sm_np_hit, sm_np_ok, sm_next_block)
                                    LLVMPositionBuilderAtEnd(builder, sm_np_ok)
                                    if sm_nested_binder != "":
                                        if sm_np_inner_type.kind == TypeKind.Unmodeled:
                                            sm_declined <- true
                                        else:
                                            sm_np_payload: LLVMValueRef = LLVMBuildExtractValue(builder, sm_np_value, 1, "smatch.np.payload")
                                            sm_np_slot: LLVMValueRef = bind_is_slot(local_scope, structs, sm_nested_binder, sm_np_inner_type, llvm_type_of(sm_np_inner_type, structs, ctx), builder)
                                            _ = LLVMBuildStore(builder, sm_np_payload, sm_np_slot)
                            elif sm_nested_payload.kind == TypeKind.Unmodeled or not is_integer_type(sm_nested_payload):
                                sm_declined <- true
                            else:
                                sm_nested_llvm: LLVMTypeRef = llvm_type_of(sm_nested_payload, structs, ctx)
                                sm_nested_pointer: LLVMValueRef = LLVMBuildStructGEP2(builder, llvm_type_of(sm_scrutinee_type, structs, ctx), sm_penum_slot, 1, "smatch.nested.ptr")
                                sm_nested_value: LLVMValueRef = LLVMBuildLoad2(builder, sm_nested_llvm, sm_nested_pointer, "smatch.nested")
                                sm_nested_hit: mutable LLVMValueRef = zeroed
                                sm_nested_first: mutable bool = true
                                for sm_nested_path in sm_nested_paths |sm_nested_hit, sm_nested_first, sm_declined, sm_nested_value, sm_nested_llvm, structs, ctx, builder|:
                                    sm_nested_ordinal: mutable i64 = penum_variant_index_of_path(sm_nested_path, structs)
                                    if sm_nested_ordinal < 0:
                                        sm_nested_ordinal <- ordinal_of_dotted_path(sm_nested_path, structs)
                                    if sm_nested_ordinal < 0:
                                        sm_declined <- true
                                    else:
                                        sm_nested_cmp: LLVMValueRef = LLVMBuildICmp(builder, 32, sm_nested_value, LLVMConstInt(sm_nested_llvm, sm_nested_ordinal.u64(), 0), "smatch.nested.eq")
                                        if sm_nested_first:
                                            sm_nested_hit <- sm_nested_cmp
                                            sm_nested_first <- false
                                        else:
                                            sm_nested_hit <- LLVMBuildOr(builder, sm_nested_hit, sm_nested_cmp, "smatch.nested.or")
                                if not sm_declined:
                                    sm_nested_ok: LLVMBasicBlockRef = LLVMAppendBasicBlockInContext(ctx, sm_function, "smatch.nested.ok")
                                    _ = LLVMBuildCondBr(builder, sm_nested_hit, sm_nested_ok, sm_next_block)
                                    LLVMPositionBuilderAtEnd(builder, sm_nested_ok)
                        continue if sm_declined
                        if sm_as_name != "":
                            sm_whole_slot: LLVMValueRef = bind_is_slot(local_scope, structs, sm_as_name, sm_scrutinee_type, llvm_type_of(sm_scrutinee_type, structs, ctx), builder)
                            _ = LLVMBuildStore(builder, sm_scrutinee_raw, sm_whole_slot)
                        # `Shape.Circle(r):` — spill-and-load the single payload field so the
                        # arm body can read `r`, exactly as the value-position emitter does.
                        if sm_penum and sm_payload_binding != "":
                            sm_payload_type: ValueType = penum_payload_of_path(sm_payload_path, structs)
                            if sm_payload_type.kind == TypeKind.Unmodeled:
                                sm_declined <- true
                            else:
                                sm_payload_pointer: LLVMValueRef = LLVMBuildStructGEP2(builder, llvm_type_of(sm_scrutinee_type, structs, ctx), sm_penum_slot, 1, "smatch.payload.ptr")
                                sm_payload_value: LLVMValueRef = LLVMBuildLoad2(builder, llvm_type_of(sm_payload_type, structs, ctx), sm_payload_pointer, "smatch.payload")
                                sm_payload_storage: mutable darray[u8] = []
                                _ = sm_payload_storage
                                sm_payload_slot: LLVMValueRef = bind_is_slot(local_scope, structs, sm_payload_binding, sm_payload_type, llvm_type_of(sm_payload_type, structs, ctx), builder)
                                _ = LLVMBuildStore(builder, sm_payload_value, sm_payload_slot)
                        # `Shape.Rect(w, h):` — load the field tuple and bind each field.
                        if sm_penum and sm_payload_multi.count > 1:
                            sm_multi_slot: i64 = penum_slot_of_path(sm_payload_path, structs)
                            if sm_multi_slot < 0:
                                sm_declined <- true
                            else:
                                sm_multi_tuple: LLVMTypeRef = penum_field_tuple_type(sm_multi_slot.usize(), structs, ctx)
                                sm_multi_pointer: LLVMValueRef = LLVMBuildStructGEP2(builder, llvm_type_of(sm_scrutinee_type, structs, ctx), sm_penum_slot, 1, "smatch.payload.ptr")
                                sm_multi_value: LLVMValueRef = LLVMBuildLoad2(builder, sm_multi_tuple, sm_multi_pointer, "smatch.payload")
                                sm_multi_start: usize = structs.penum_field_type_start[sm_multi_slot.usize()]
                                for sm_multi_index in 0..<sm_payload_multi.count |sm_payload_multi, sm_multi_start, sm_multi_value, structs, local_scope, ctx, builder|:
                                    sm_multi_type: ValueType = copied_type(structs.penum_field_types[sm_multi_start + sm_multi_index])
                                    sm_multi_field_value: LLVMValueRef = LLVMBuildExtractValue(builder, sm_multi_value, sm_multi_index.u32(), "smatch.field")
                                    sm_multi_storage: mutable darray[u8] = []
                                    _ = sm_multi_storage
                                    sm_multi_field_slot: LLVMValueRef = bind_is_slot(local_scope, structs, sm_payload_multi[sm_multi_index], sm_multi_type, llvm_type_of(sm_multi_type, structs, ctx), builder)
                                    _ = LLVMBuildStore(builder, sm_multi_field_value, sm_multi_field_slot)
                        # A GUARDED arm (`Variant(x) if x > 0:` / `Ident if cond:`): payload bound
                        # above so the guard can read it; on true fall into a guarded body block,
                        # on false continue to the next arm (mirrors the match-expression emitter).
                        if not sm_declined and arm_has_guard(sm_arm.guard):
                            if emit_condition(sm_arm.guard, local_scope, fns, structs, generics, runtime, m, ctx, builder) is sm_guard_bit:
                                sm_guard_body: LLVMBasicBlockRef = LLVMAppendBasicBlockInContext(ctx, sm_function, "smatch.guard")
                                _ = LLVMBuildCondBr(builder, sm_guard_bit, sm_guard_body, sm_next_block)
                                LLVMPositionBuilderAtEnd(builder, sm_guard_body)
                            else:
                                sm_declined <- true
                        if sm_declined:
                            LLVMPositionBuilderAtEnd(builder, sm_next_block)
                        else:
                            sm_arm_status: EmitStatus = emit_statements(sm_arm.body, return_type, local_scope, loops, regions, fns, structs, generics, runtime, m, ctx, builder)
                            sm_declined <- true if sm_arm_status == EmitStatus.Declined
                            sm_any_open <- true if sm_arm_status == EmitStatus.Open
                            branch_if_open(sm_arm_status, builder, sm_done)
                            LLVMPositionBuilderAtEnd(builder, sm_next_block)
                structs.cond_bind_depth <- structs.cond_bind_depth - 1
                if structs.cond_bind_depth == 0:
                    structs.cond_bind_names <- []
                    structs.cond_bind_slots <- []
                    structs.cond_bind_types <- []
                EmitStatus.Declined return if sm_declined
                # No `_` arm: the frontend proved exhaustiveness, so a fall-through of the
                # last arm's next-block is unreachable.
                if not sm_saw_default:
                    _ = LLVMBuildUnreachable(builder)
                LLVMPositionBuilderAtEnd(builder, sm_done)
                # If every arm terminated, the done block is dead — terminate it too.
                if not sm_any_open:
                    _ = LLVMBuildUnreachable(builder)
                    return EmitStatus.Terminated
                return EmitStatus.Open
            handled <- false
            return EmitStatus.Declined

